# tele dial — the one project setting that decides what your runs compile in.
# Read fresh on every run by zrun (the runner behind your run keybinds).
# Every run prints its dial, so you always know what you're running.
#
#   off   no telemetry, nothing woven. This is what a release build ships.
#   on    lean: hand-called tele primitives active, zero auto-capture.
#   max   firehose (DEV ONLY): weave auto-captures every binding + whole-program
#         execution hooks. The heavy instrumentation — never shipped, like a
#         sanitizer/coverage build. Output is huge; use windowless → run.log.
#
# Changing the dial is a RARE action — that's why it lives here, not on a key.
# Your run keybinds (console / windowless) never change; they just honor this.
# Switch with:  just tele max   |   just tele on   |   just tele off
max
